 ## Overview
-Progressive Inpainting-and-Erasing (PERF) is a method for reconstructing a panoramic Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) from a single input panorama by iteratively synthesizing novel views and refining the 3D geometry. It solves the problem of geometry conflicts that arise when inpainting invisible regions of a scene, ensuring that the generated content remains consistent with the already-learned visible geometry. Unlike methods that optimize a static NeRF from multiple views, PERF progressively expands the viewpoint range by alternating between collaborative RGBD inpainting of new views and erasing geometrically inconsistent regions from the training supervision [S1].
+Progressive Inpainting-and-Erasing (PERF) is a method for reconstructing a panoramic Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) from a single input panorama by iteratively expanding the view coverage through novel view synthesis and geometry-aware training [S1]. It solves the problem of geometry conflicts that arise when inpainting invisible regions with generative models, which may produce structures inconsistent with the already-learned visible geometry [S1]. Unlike methods that optimize a fixed set of views, PERF progressively enlarges the range of viewpoints, using a conflict mask to erase inconsistent regions from supervision before fine-tuning the NeRF [S1].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A single RGB panorama image $I_{rgb}$.
-*   **Output:** A panoramic NeRF representation $f_{nerf}$, implemented using Instant-NGP [S1].
+*   **Input:** A single input panorama image $I_{rgb}$ [S1].
+*   **Output:** A panoramic NeRF representation $f_{nerf}$ [S1].
 
 **Data Structures:**
